 //  of the instruction token.
 
+// INSTRUCTION_UNASSIGNED is a token value that no D3D9 instruction uses: its opcode_string is NULL, it has no state and NO EMITTER (the profile
+//  tables get zeros). Rule (the table row is the whole proof): parse_instruction_token (mojoshader.c) returns on `opcode_string == NULL`
+//  ("Unknown opcode.") before it reads or calls the emitter, and the emitter pointer is read from this table only, so an emitter for such a
+//  row could never run. Every row of the table with a NULL opcode_string is written with this macro, and only those.
 // INSTRUCTION_STATE means this opcode has to update the state machine
 //  (we're entering an ELSE block, etc). INSTRUCTION means there's no
